        {
            "number": 4,
            "revision": "3f5fbfd291c112c31660d21e438724e6023d81f4",
            "parents": [
                "437857c521f0836d6dc15e93699a3c58e0f2eae0"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/39/88839/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Manish Tiwari",
                "email": "tmanish.in+openbmc@gmail.com",
                "username": "manishtwari"
            },
            "createdOn": 1775721603,
            "author": {
                "name": "Manish Tiwari",
                "email": "tmanish.in+openbmc@gmail.com",
                "username": "manishtwari"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/entry_points.cpp",
                    "line": 84,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Since this never ended up being needed, can we just drop it?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/entry_points.cpp",
                    "line": 84,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "+1"
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/entry_points.cpp",
                    "line": 84,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Manish Tiwari",
                        "email": "tmanish.in+openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manishtwari"
                    },
                    "message": "Cannot drop it, the two-parameter signature is required to match ExtensionLogAssociation type. Removing it would cause the function to register as DeleteFunction instead.\n\nHowever, I can drop the objectPath parameter from the inner function call in commit https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-logging/+/88887 where it's passed as:\n```\nmanager->linkPELToEventLog(obmcId, objectPath);\n```\nSince it only takes obmcLogID, that second parameter can be removed from the call."
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/entry_points.cpp",
                    "line": 84,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "But its different vector, right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/entry_points.cpp",
                    "line": 84,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Manish Tiwari",
                        "email": "tmanish.in+openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manishtwari"
                    },
                    "message": "They are stored in different vectors, but the selection happens earlier based on the callback signature.\n\n`REGISTER_EXTENSION_FUNCTION(pelEntryRestored)` currently registers this as an ExtensionLogAssociation: `std::function<void(uint32_t, const std::string&)>`\n\nIf I remove `objectPath`, the callback becomes `std::function<void(uint32_t)>`, which matches `DeleteFunction` instead.\n\nThat also creates a constructor overload conflict, since Extensions has constructors for both callback types.\n\nSo the second parameter is still needed to keep this registered under the correct extension hook."
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/entry_points.cpp",
                    "line": 84,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks, I had forgotten all about that."
                }
            ],
            "files": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "type": "ADDED",
                    "insertions": 20,
                    "deletions": 0
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions.cpp",
